Wildfires have broken out across southern France, forcing evacuations and stretching firefighting teams as the country prepares for the third heatwave of the summer, with the country's forests under increasing threat from climate change and disputes over logging.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76a15890-75f0-11f1-ae1f-a949136140ad</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 13:36:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cb5bc50-75ff-11f1-9c62-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8Z872N.jpg">AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>World Bank drops climate funding target, raising fears for Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260702-world-bank-drops-climate-funding-target-raising-fears-for-africa</link><description>
The World Bank has abandoned its target of directing 45 percent of its financing to projects that help tackle climate change, prompting warnings that poorer countries – especially in Africa – could receive less support to adapt to a warming world.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b91adfd8-7538-11f1-9bc1-c774f26789d8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 10:43:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/16c63082-95a9-11ee-894a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23341508788290.jpg">AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Paris death penalty congress warns abolition cannot be taken for granted</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260702-macron-warns-death-penalty-debate-is-back-as-executions-rise-worldwide</link><description>
The fight to abolish the death penalty remains "eminently contemporary", French President Emmanuel Macron said as campaigners, judges and former death row prisoners gathered in Paris this week for the World Congress Against the Death Penalty, amid rising executions worldwide and renewed support for capital punishment in some democracies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f30e478e-7524-11f1-b65e-7129b96364f7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 09:44:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b3af01e-75fa-11f1-9faa-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP080527047676.jpg">ASSOCIATED PRESS - Pat Sullivan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on France</category><title>Podcast: Adapting to heat, France's fitness boom, Paris Mosque at 100</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-france/20260702-podcast-climate-adaptation-heatwave-fitness-paris-mosque-algeria-france</link><description>
As France's record-breaking heatwave last week raises questions about how the country will have to adapt to a warming climate, we look at what that could mean for French culture. We also explore the country's growing interest in fitness – driven in part by its most popular YouTuber – and examine how the Grand Mosque of Paris, which marks its centenary this year, became both a symbol of Islam in France and a recurring source of political tension.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df34bd66-7609-11f1-9f4c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/episode-spotlight-on-france-episode-148-red.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">34686256-760a-11f1-bf8b-a7557f473b29</guid><pubDate>Thu, 02 Jul 2026 14:30:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Senegal midfielder Gueye refuses to play while coaching staff stay in charge</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260702-senegal-midfielder-gueye-refuses-to-play-while-coaching-staff-stay-in-charge-world-cup-2026</link><description>
